	I played around with your idea of having different flavors,
but I didn't really get anywhere.  


	Option 1:  make the flavors match those of actual monsters,
leaving out the instakill ones.  

   o  Intrinsics.  Give "black dragon flavored" rations half the 
      normal chance of granting the intrinsic.  This makes it a 
      bit easier to gain intrinsics, but not by much:  you see tins
      in the early game, but few rations.  (If rebalancing is needed,
      cut back on the odds of gaining intrinsics by eating monster
      flesh.)

   o  Vegan monks have less food around.  (Minor.)

   o  C and K rations no longer stack.  (Minor.)

	OK, it's different, but I don't see that it adds much to the
game.  (It does fit in very well with a YANI of mine; if I ever
implement "intrinsics time out", I'll swipe your idea then.)


	Option 2:  use flavors from outside the game.  "Porcupine
flavored".  Use the hallucination monster names when the player is 
off his nut.  "Microscopic space fleet flavored".

	This would be entertaining.  (At least, it would be enter-
taining if *I* named the flavors.)  Are you willing to write a 
patch for it, or this YANI falling off the edge of the universe?
(If you aren't a coder, scream at me to write that "how-to" guide
I sometimes mumble about.)

	You could fit a lot of YAFMs around this fairly easily.  "Yum,
sea monster flavored:  your favorite".  "Sheesh, manufactured monkey
meat AGAIN?"  "These puppy dog tails need more salt."


	Option 3:  use reasonable real-world flavors.  "Beef flavor-
ed".

	Dull.  It adds the least little smidgen to the game, but
not enough to notice.


